CVPR-2025-P0044,CVPR-2025-A000255,Yue Chen,shared,3,5,5,"Zhejiang University Westlake University University of Tübingen, Tübingen AI Center Max Planck Institute for Informatics, Saarland Informatics Campus Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems fanegg.github.io/Feat2GS BagBag of VFM Features Features Bagof ofVFM VFM Features Stable StableDiffusion Diffusion view view view DINO DINO DINO Stable Diffusion Feat2GS Feat2GS Feat2GS Readout Readout Readout NVS NVS NVS RADIO RADIO RADIO RADIO RADIO RADIO InstantSplat InstantSplat InstantSplat MAE MAE MAE MAE MAE MAE … … … view view view DUSt3R DUSt3R DUSt3R Readout Readout Readout … … … shared weight shared weight shared weight view view view MiDaS MiDaS MiDaS SAM SAM SAM DINOv2 DINOv2 DINOv2 CLIP CLIP CLIP …… … Texture Texture Texture shared weight shared weight shared weight MASt3R MASt3R MAE MAE MAE MASt3R RADIO RADIO RADIO Geometry Geometry Geometry Readout Readout Readout Geometry Texture Geometry Geometry Texture Texture (a) Feat2GS as VFM Probe (b) Extensive Analysis of VFM Ours Ours Ours (c) Strong Baseline Figure . We present Feat2GS, a unified framework to probe “texture and geometry awareness” of visual foundation models (VFMs). Novel-view synthesis (NVS) serves as an effective proxy for 3D evaluation. (a) Casually captured photos are input into VFMs to extract features and into a stereo reconstructor to obtain relative poses. Pixel-wise features are transformed into 3D Gaussians (3DGS) using a lightweight readout layer trained with photometric loss. (b) 3DGS parameters, grouped into Geometry and Texture, enable separate analysis of geometry/texture awareness in VFMs, evaluated by the NVS quality on diverse, unposed open-world images. (c) Our baseline derived from extensive empirical analysis, achieves superior performance for NVS by simply concatenating features from diverse VFMs.",-17,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P0044.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Chen_Feat2GS_Probing_Visual_Foundation_Models_with_Gaussian_Splatting_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
