CVPR-2025-P0051,CVPR-2025-A000298,Jihyun Lee,shared,3,10,10,"Codec Avatars Lab, Meta (a) Egocentric KAIST Imperial College London whole-body tracking results. Input Estimated Pose GT Pose Input Estimated Pose (a) Egocentric whole-body motion estimation results. GT Pose (b) Avatar driving example. Figure . Real-time and high-fidelity whole-body motion estimation from stereo egocentric images. We propose R EWIND, a novel egocentric image-conditioned diffusion model for high-quality 3D whole-body motion estimation. R EWIND is real-time, causal, and generalizable to unseen motion lengths, making it seamlessly applicable for driving photorealistic avatars or meshes. Please refer to the supplementary video, which demonstrates that R EWIND estimates significantly more plausible motions compared to existing methods.",2,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P0051.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Lee_REWIND_Real-Time_Egocentric_Whole-Body_Motion_Diffusion_with_Exemplar-Based_Identity_Conditioning_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
