CVPR-2025-P0108,CVPR-2025-A000712,Xi Wang,shared,3,4,4,"LIX, École Polytechnique, IP Paris Univ Rennes, IRISA, Inria, CNRS Figure . While current state-of-the-art video generation approaches offer limited control to users on camera motion, we propose a dedicated data augmentation framework —AKiRa — to train an optical video generation model that provides users with a panel of controls on camera motions (top row), camera focal length (second row), lens distortion (third row), or bokeh (camera aperture and focus in bottom row). See more on our project page:",-6,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P0108.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wang_AKiRa_Augmentation_Kit_on_Rays_for_Optical_Video_Generation_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
