CVPR-2025-P0374,CVPR-2025-A002335,Huangyue Yu,shared,3,12,12,"State Key Laboratory of General Artificial Intelligence, BIGAI Tsinghua University Beijing Institute of Technology University of Science and Technology of China Figure . Overview of M ETA S CENES, a large-scale simulatable 3D scene dataset constructed by replacing objects in real-world 3D scans with realistic and high-quality object assets retrieved or reconstructed from diverse sources. strate that this process heavily relies on artist-driven designs, which demand substantial human effort and present significant scalability challenges. To scalably produce realistic and interactive 3D scenes, we first present M ETA S CENES, a large-scale simulatable 3D scene dataset constructed from real-world scans, which includes objects spanning fine-grained categories. Then, we introduce S CAN 2S IM, a robust multi-modal alignment model, which enables the automated, high-quality replacement of assets, thereby eliminating the reliance on artist-driven designs for scaling",1,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P0374.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Yu_METASCENES_Towards_Automated_Replica_Creation_for_Real-world_3D_Scans_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
