CVPR-2025-P0471,CVPR-2025-A002958,Hoon-Gyu Chung,shared,3,3,3,". . (a) Input multi-view flash images (b) Image and normals under novel view and lighting (c) Our interpretable basis BRDFs and weight maps (d) Reflectance editing with environment relighting Figure . We propose a differentiable inverse rendering method with (a) multi-view flash photography inputs. Our analysis-by-synthesis method achieves not only (b) novel-view relighting and accurate geometry reconstruction, but also (c) interpretable basis BRDFs and their spatially-separated weights. This allows for (d) intuitive scene editing.",-6,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P0471.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Chung_Differentiable_Inverse_Rendering_with_Interpretable_Basis_BRDFs_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
