CVPR-2025-P1220,CVPR-2025-A007673,Chen-Wei Chang,shared,3,7,7,"National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University MediaTek Inc. Extracting illumination’s RGB color Color checker inpainting Achromatic squares Input image Image with an inpainted color checker Angular error: . Inpainted color checker Color cast removed Output image with color cast removed Angular error: . Inpainted color checker Color cast removed Angular error: . Inpainted color checker Color cast removed Figure . Our method performs color constancy through diffusion-based color checker inpainting. (top left) Given an input image, we first inpaint a color checker with Stable Diffusion, aligning the achromatic (gray) squares to accurately reflect the scene illumination (top middle). The RGB color extracted from the achromatic squares is then used to remove the color cast from the input image (top right). (Bottom) Our approach leverages the strong priors of pre-trained diffusion models to accurately estimate scene illumination without requiring physical color checkers during capture, enabling accurate white balance correction across diverse scenes. . Introduction",-2,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1220.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Chang_GCC_Generative_Color_Constancy_via_Diffusing_a_Color_Checker_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
