CVPR-2025-P1255,CVPR-2025-A007891,Chaoyang Wang,shared,3,10,10,"Snap Inc Umass Amherst KAUST Time 4D Video Diffusion Model Output View Input freeze-time video Input fixed-view video Real-World Capture “move a truck towards right” “a yellow lego brick turns into a cat” Figure . 4Real-Video is a 4D generation framework that (top-left) takes a fixed-view video and a freeze-time video as input and generates a grid of consistent video frames. One axis of the grid varies in time, and the other axis varies the viewpoint. The input videos can be real videos or videos generated by a video model. Note that our method can generate grids larger than × videos. Here, we present subsets of frames as an example. (top-right) 4D videos generated from generated videos. (bottom) We can also capture a real-world scene, and generate a 4D video given different prompts.",-4,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1255.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wang_4Real-Video_Learning_Generalizable_Photo-Realistic_4D_Video_Diffusion_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
