CVPR-2025-P1266,CVPR-2025-A007975,Yao-Chih Lee,shared,3,7,7,"Google DeepMind University of Maryland College Park Weizmann Institute of Science See-through foreground ActionShot (duplicating + retiming) Layer resizing + background replacement Input video Object removal Output: Omnimatte layers Layer editing Figure . Generative Omnimatte. Our method decomposes a video into a set of RGBA omnimatte layers, where each layer consists of a fully-visible object and its associated effects like shadows and reflections. We improve upon existing work by adding a generative video prior, allowing our method to complete occluded regions (top, middle) and handle dynamic backgrounds (bottom).",-1,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1266.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Lee_Generative_Omnimatte_Learning_to_Decompose_Video_into_Layers_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
