CVPR-2025-P1461,CVPR-2025-A009127,Youyu Chen,shared,3,7,7,"Harbin Institute of Technology Huawei Noah’s Ark Lab Figure . We propose DashGaussian, a fast 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) optimization method that can be easily plugged into existing 3DGS backbones. DashGaussian significantly boosts the training speed of various 3DGS backbones by . % on average without trading off rendering quality. Equipping DashGaussian to prior-art 3DGS methods, we reduce the optimization time of a 3DGS model with millions of primitives to seconds on a consumer-grade GPU. The figures above show the scene “stump” in the Mip-NeRF dataset. . Introduction",-2,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1461.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Chen_DashGaussian_Optimizing_3D_Gaussian_Splatting_in_200_Seconds_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
