CVPR-2025-P1530,CVPR-2025-A009533,Yueru Jia,shared,3,11,11,"Attention Place bottle at rack Pour water Unplug charge MetaWorld (MuJoCo, Gripper) Stack blocks Pick and place Slide block Adroit (MuJoCo, Dexterous hands) Water plants Wipe table Open drawer… RLBench (CoppelaSim, Gripper) b) Explicit 3D robotic representation 2D Position Embedding Policy Head 2D Foundation Model Robot State Reconstructing Depth Guide MAE Decoder Point Cloud a) Implicit 3D robotic representation 2D Foundation Model Image State Key Laboratory of Multimedia Information Processing, School of Computer Science, Peking University; Beijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence (BAAI); CUHK Project web page: lift3d-web.github.io Execution Left part: Overview of our proposed Lift3D Right part: Extensive evaluation on simulation and real-world tasks. Figure . Lift3D empowers 2D foundation models with 3D manipulation capabilities by refining implicit 3D robotic representations through task-related affordance masking and depth reconstruction, while enhancing explicit 3D robotic representations by leveraging the pretrained 2D positional embeddings to encode point cloud. Lift3D achieves robustness and surprising effectiveness in diverse simulation and real-world tasks.",1,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1530.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Jia_Lift3D_Policy_Lifting_2D_Foundation_Models_for_Robust_3D_Robotic_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
