CVPR-2025-P1558,CVPR-2025-A009713,Jianwei Yang,shared,3,12,12,"Microsoft Research, University of Maryland, University of Wisconsin-Madison KAIST, University of Washington User: What is they doing? Physical Environment User: On what date did the individual leave a place that Simon thought was very important to him? User: Close the middle drawer Magma: They are camping in a forest and hiking on a rocky mountain. Magma: The date is June , . Task: Push the chip bag to left Task: Put the can to left Task: Peel the potato Task: Stir the food in the pot Magma: Trajectory Rollout on SimplerEnv Google Robot Temporal User: The figure represents a 5x5 grid containing various animals, where each 1x1 square is considered a block and each block contains an animal from ['cat', 'dog', 'elephant', 'giraffe', 'rabbit']. What is the animal of the block located at the first row, second column of the grid? User: Pick up the mushroom to the pot Magma: Trajectory Rollout on Widow-X Real Robot Planning M Magma: The animal is a cat. Spatial User: What is unusual thing about this image? Magma: The unusual aspect of this image is that a man is ironing clothes on the back of a yellow taxi. …. User: Find baby shoes under dollars and rated stars. Magma: Trajectory on Mind2Web Task: Plan a visit to the museum User: How to increase the sound? Magma: Tap on the ""Volume"" icon. Then, slide the volume up to increase the volume. Digital Environment Task: Lock Screen Multimodal Understanding Task: View my Account Multimodal Action Grounding Task: Install app ""Instagram"" Magma: Trajectory on AITW Multimodal Agentic Taks Figure . We introduce Magma, the first foundation model that is capable of interpreting and grounding multimodal inputs, and taking actions towards a goal in both digital and physical environments. With our newly proposed pretraining techniques, Magma learns effectively from images, videos and robotics data to bridge verbal and spatial intelligence, taking a step further to an intelligent multimodal AI agent. beled by Trace-of-Mark (ToM) for action planning. Extensive experiments show that SoM and ToM help bridge the gap between verbal and action abilities and significantly enhance spatio-temporal intelligence which is fundamental to agentic tasks, as shown in Fig. . In particular, Magma creates new state-of-the-art results on UI navigation and robotic manipulation tasks, outperforming previous models that are specifically tailored to these tasks. Moreover, Magma preserves strong multimodal understanding ability and compares favorably to popular large multimodal models that are trained on much larger datasets. We have made our model and code public for reproducibility1 .",3,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1558.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Yang_Magma_A_Foundation_Model_for_Multimodal_AI_Agents_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
