CVPR-2025-P1962,CVPR-2025-A012257,Tianyu Wang,shared,3,10,10,"Adobe Research The Chinese University of Hong Kong [I] Object Relocation Image with Object Mask [II] Object Removal with Shadow Shadow Removal Result Shadow Detection and Removal ( ) MetaShadow Three-in-One Model ( ) ( ) ( ) [III] Object Insertion with Shadow Relocate Object Shadow Synthesis Image with Synthesized Shadows Image with Relocated Objects (a) (b) (c) Figure . MetaShadow is a versatile three-in-one framework designed for shadow-related tasks, enabling shadow manipulation in various object-centered image editing operations such as: [I] Object Relocation: Our model can detect and remove the shadow of an existing object, then synthesize the shadow in the new location consistent with the original shadow. [II] Remove an object and its shadow: ( ) Based on the mask of the unwanted object, our model can directly remove its shadow ( ). After removing the object ( ), we can eliminate any remaining shadows for a cleaner background ( ) if we do not specify which shadow to remove. [III] Insert an object and synthesize its shadow: When inserting the person in (b) to another image (a) with similar lighting, our model can generate a realistic shadow, enhancing the final compositing quality.",0,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P1962.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wang_MetaShadow_Object-Centered_Shadow_Detection_Removal_and_Synthesis_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
