CVPR-2025-P2018,CVPR-2025-A012596,Bingliang Zhang,shared,3,6,6,"California Institute of Technology NVIDIA Stanford University OpenAI Figure . Overview of Decoupled Annealing Posterior Sampling (DAPS). Our method provides a flexible and effective framework for solving inverse problems through a decoupled posterior sampling process. In (a)(b), we present DAPS visual results on FFHQ and ImageNet at a resolution of , and in (c), on natural images at a resolution of . In (d), we display DAPS results on compressed sensing multi-coil MRI (CS-MRI). DAPS effectively addresses nonlinear inverse problems as well as medical imaging MRI challenges. Additionally, DAPS can be enhanced using large-scale latent diffusion models (LDMs) [",-2,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2018.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Zhang_Improving_Diffusion_Inverse_Problem_Solving_with_Decoupled_Noise_Annealing_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
