CVPR-2025-P2249,CVPR-2025-A014005,Yujie Wang,shared,3,3,3,"State Key Laboratory of General Artificial Intelligence, Peking University School of Intelligence Science and Technology, Peking University University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill Post-Capture Control Novel View Synthesis Input Images with Defocus Blur Mip-Splatting Ours Aperture Focal Distance Ours (DOF Rendering) (a) (b) (c) (d) Figure . Our method enhances 3DGS with a finite-aperture camera model and differentiable depth-of-field (DOF) rendering, enabling post-capture DOF control after training and capturing natural defocus cues from multi-view defocused images. Differentiable DOF rendering also mitigates reconstruction artifacts caused by multi-view inconsistent defocus blur. Insets (a)-(d), with in-focus areas in pink, show images rendered under various settings: (a)-(c) share aperture but differ in focal distance; (d) matches (b)’s focal distance but has a larger aperture.",-9,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2249.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wang_DOF-GS_Adjustable_Depth-of-Field_3D_Gaussian_Splatting_for_Post-Capture_Refocusing_Defocus_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
CVPR-2025-P2249,CVPR-2025-A014006,Praneeth Chakravarthula,shared,3,3,3,"State Key Laboratory of General Artificial Intelligence, Peking University School of Intelligence Science and Technology, Peking University University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill Post-Capture Control Novel View Synthesis Input Images with Defocus Blur Mip-Splatting Ours Aperture Focal Distance Ours (DOF Rendering) (a) (b) (c) (d) Figure . Our method enhances 3DGS with a finite-aperture camera model and differentiable depth-of-field (DOF) rendering, enabling post-capture DOF control after training and capturing natural defocus cues from multi-view defocused images. Differentiable DOF rendering also mitigates reconstruction artifacts caused by multi-view inconsistent defocus blur. Insets (a)-(d), with in-focus areas in pink, show images rendered under various settings: (a)-(c) share aperture but differ in focal distance; (d) matches (b)’s focal distance but has a larger aperture.",-9,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2249.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wang_DOF-GS_Adjustable_Depth-of-Field_3D_Gaussian_Splatting_for_Post-Capture_Refocusing_Defocus_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
CVPR-2025-P2249,CVPR-2025-A014007,Baoquan Chen,shared,3,3,3,"State Key Laboratory of General Artificial Intelligence, Peking University School of Intelligence Science and Technology, Peking University University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill Post-Capture Control Novel View Synthesis Input Images with Defocus Blur Mip-Splatting Ours Aperture Focal Distance Ours (DOF Rendering) (a) (b) (c) (d) Figure . Our method enhances 3DGS with a finite-aperture camera model and differentiable depth-of-field (DOF) rendering, enabling post-capture DOF control after training and capturing natural defocus cues from multi-view defocused images. Differentiable DOF rendering also mitigates reconstruction artifacts caused by multi-view inconsistent defocus blur. Insets (a)-(d), with in-focus areas in pink, show images rendered under various settings: (a)-(c) share aperture but differ in focal distance; (d) matches (b)’s focal distance but has a larger aperture.",-9,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2249.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wang_DOF-GS_Adjustable_Depth-of-Field_3D_Gaussian_Splatting_for_Post-Capture_Refocusing_Defocus_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
