CVPR-2025-P2470,CVPR-2025-A015313,Lihan Jiang,shared,3,9,9,"University of Science and Technology of China, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Brown University, The University of Hong Kong, CPII Figure . Horizon-GS enables high-quality rendering and reconstruction of aerial-to-ground scenes with unprecedented fidelity across scales, supporting drastic view changes. The colored camera trajectories in the center illustrate the novel viewpoints, while the reconstructed mesh is overlaid on the scene. The surrounding images show the corresponding predicted images for each viewpoint. Explore more demos on our project page: perspectives with a new training strategy, overcoming viewpoint discrepancies to generate high-fidelity scenes. We also curate a high-quality aerial-to-ground views dataset encompassing both synthetic and real-world scene to advance further research. Experiments across diverse urban scene datasets confirm the effectiveness of our method.",1,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2470.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Jiang_Horizon-GS_Unified_3D_Gaussian_Splatting_for_Large-Scale_Aerial-to-Ground_Scenes_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
