CVPR-2025-P2495,CVPR-2025-A015473,Ozgur Kara,shared,3,6,6,"UIUC Adobe Project Webpage: ""a woman knits on the couch in a warm living room"" ""a man plays the guitar in his music room"" ""a woman sits at a kitchen table, softly illuminated by morning light as she glances out the window"" ""a man sketches in a notebook at a quiet cafe, his hand moving quickly across the page"" Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- Shot- ""she then organizes clothes in a walk in closet"" ""he then records a song on his laptop, listening with headphones"" ""she sips her coffee, her eyes drifting thoughtfully across the room"" ""he pauses, looking up thoughtfully before continuing his drawing"" ""the woman then begins to eat a simple meal, her movements slow and deliberate"" ""later, the man steps outside, his notebook tucked under his arm as he takes in the city around him"" Figure . ShotAdapter is a lightweight framework that enables text-to-multi-shot video generation by fine-tuning a pre-trained textto-video model. It allows control over number and duration of shots as well as shot content through shot-specific text prompts. The framework maintains character identity while being able to preserve backgrounds (e.g. 3rd row) or transition to new ones (e.g. 4th row), featuring distinct activities (e.g. playing guitar, then using laptop) and perspectives.",-4,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2495.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Kara_ShotAdapter_Text-to-Multi-Shot_Video_Generation_with_Diffusion_Models_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
