CVPR-2025-P2527,CVPR-2025-A015673,Xiaoyang Wu,shared,3,10,10,"The University of Hong Kong Meta Reality Labs Research S3DIS -Fold Sem. Seg. S3DIS Sem. Seg. D: ScanNet++ Sem. Seg. . . . ScanNet200 Ins. Seg. . ScanNet Ins. Seg. ScanNet200 Sem. Seg. . . . . . Sonata . . ScanNet Eff. L.S. % Sem.KITTI Sem. Seg. PTv3 MSC D: SSL Pretext Tasks D: Encoder ScanNet Sem. Seg. concatenate up-cast attention PC ScanNet Eff. L.A. . % - MSC ScanNet .3x stronger . % - Sonata SparseUNet Self-distillation Perception PCA pooling . % - DINOv2 ScanNet Eff. L.S. % PointContrast Flexible Task Heads D: Decoder-free . ScanNet Eff. L.A. ScanNet++ . Ins. Seg. Waymo Sem. Seg. Linear Probing … D: . D: D: K-means Linear Probing Dense Matching Sparse Matching Local View Semantic Awareness Spatial Reasoning Figure . Main properties. Sonata leads to reliable 3D self-supervised pretraining with the following superior and emerging properties: . Perception. Sonata advances state-of-the-art results across 3D indoor and outdoor perception tasks; . Linear probing. With less than . % learnable parameters, Sonata achieves strong and usable linear probing performance which is . → better than previous SOTA; . Decoder-free. Sonata moves beyond the inflexible U-Net structure, offering multi-scale representations that unchain future 3D research from previous architectural constraints. . Semantic awareness. Sonata reveals semantic structure in PCA and K-means visualizations. . Spatial reasoning. Sonata allows spatial correspondence even under strong augmentations as visualized via feature similarity.",-3,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2527.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Wu_Sonata_Self-Supervised_Learning_of_Reliable_Point_Representations_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
