CVPR-2025-P2535,CVPR-2025-A015732,Wenqiao Li,shared,3,7,7,"ShanghaiTech University University of Michigan, Ann Arbor Monash University (a) Object (b) Interaction Rubber Band Gear Assembly Bottled Water Abnormal Normal Abnormal Normal Abnormal Normal (c) Video with Physical Dynamics t Water Leak Misalignment Crack Figure . Towards visual discrimination of physical dynamics in real-world industrial object anomaly detection. We illustrate objects, interactions, and time-sequenced videos from the Physics-Grounded Anomaly Detection dataset: (a) Object; (b) Interaction: Applied actions shown with directional arrows; (c) Video with Physical Dynamics: Temporal sequences showing normal and abnormal states, highlighting anomalies like leaks, misalignments, and cracks. By focusing on the dynamic behaviors of complex objects, we enhance understanding of interactions and failure modes in real-world settings, where both structure and motion contribute to anomaly detection.",-7,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2535.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Li_Towards_Visual_Discrimination_and_Reasoning_of_Real-World_Physical_Dynamics_Physics-Grounded_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
