CVPR-2025-P2537,CVPR-2025-A015744,Hanzhe Hu,shared,3,9,9,"Adobe Research a chihuahua lying in a pool ring Reconstruction Transformer Diffusion Transformer ... ... ... .32s MV Latents Latent -step -view Diffusion a panda wearing a chef's hat and kneading bread dough on a countertop a plush toy of a corgi nurse a cake in the shape of a train ... .03s Latent GS-LRM a bichon frise wearing academic regalia a raccoon stealing a pie Campsite with a tent on grassy ground, a backpack against it, a campfire surrounded by stones. A sleeping bag partially unrolled next to the tent, a lantern hanging from a tree branch a goat drinking beer a badger wearing a party hat and blowing out birthday candles on a cake a lion reading the newspaper Figure . Overview of our Turbo3D text-to-3D system. Turbo3D generates high-quality 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) assets from user prompts in less than second on a single A100 GPU. It’s a two-stage pipeline consisting of a highly efficient latent-space few-step multi-view (MV) generator and single-step MV reconstructor. Note that we visualize latents as RGB images and 3DGS assets as point clouds in the pipeline figure for clarity.",-4,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2537.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Hu_Turbo3D_Ultra-fast_Text-to-3D_Generation_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
