CVPR-2025-P2681,CVPR-2025-A016594,Alexander Pondaven,shared,3,5,5,"MBZUAI ditflow.github.io Reference DiT DiT DiTFlow A lion walking through a busy market Robot walking on a sidewalk Motorbiker driving around moonlit sand dunes Astronaut walking on the moon Figure . Overview of DiTFlow. We propose a motion transfer method tailored for video Diffusion Transformers (DiT). We exploit a training-free strategy to transfer the motion of a reference video (top) to newly synthesized video content with arbitrary prompts (bottom). By optimizing DiT-specific positional embeddings, we can also synthesize new videos in a zero-shot manner.",-6,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2681.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Pondaven_Video_Motion_Transfer_with_Diffusion_Transformers_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
