CVPR-2025-P2812,CVPR-2025-A017421,Guangzhao He,shared,3,4,4,"Decoder Edited Blobs Blobs Edited Result Edited Result Figure . We introduce Category-Agnostic Neural Object Rigging (CANOR), a novel approach that learns to discover a low-dimensional pose space for dynamic objects. The representation is learned from animated 3D sequences of a deformable object category in an unsupervised fashion without relying on any category-specific expert knowledge. By decomposing each object’s geometry into a sparse set of feature-embedded blobs, CANOR enables intuitive manipulation of object poses by editing the blobs. This representation captures interpretable motion structures for a diverse range of dynamic object categories.",-6,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2812.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/He_Category-Agnostic_Neural_Object_Rigging_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
