CVPR-2025-P2868,CVPR-2025-A017767,Ding Ding,shared,3,8,8,"Wuhan University Xi’an Jiaotong University University of Science and Technology of China Microsoft Research Asia Stage : Pixel Propagation Stage : Content Generation The state-of-the-art method Flow-based Warping HomoGen Flow Consistency Check Pasting Content Generation in VT without consistency check or hand-crafted filtering operation Input with Mask Homography Registration Content Generation in VDM Figure . Two-stage pipelines of HomoGen and the state-of-the-art method. Previous flow-based propagation warps pixels across frames, followed by a video transformer (VT) that generates remaining missing content. In contrast, HomoGen’s homography-based propagation warps pixels as priors to control content generation in a video diffusion model (VDM) that filters out artifacts in the priors during denoising.",-3,data/raw/cvpr/2025/first_pages/CVPR-2025-P2868.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2025/papers/Ding_HomoGen_Enhanced_Video_Inpainting_via_Homography_Propagation_and_Diffusion_CVPR_2025_paper.pdf
